    {
      "field_name": "other_symptoms_established",
      "value": "apnea; oxygen desaturation; dusky blue discoloration; EEG slowing; heart rate changes",
      "quote": "new spells of paroxysmal leg jerking and apnea. Determination of blood gases on blood drawn from an indwelling arterial line during the course of these two spells showed that the patient had significantly desaturated arterial oxygen concentration (Table 1). After she was placed back in bed, the leg shaking continued; she fanned herself with her hands, uttered words such as “fan me,” and was able to count while becoming progressively dusky blue in the face, fingers, and toes. The electroencephalogram showed generalized slowing of the background to 5-6 Hz, consistent with the patient’s hypoxemia at this stage.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
