    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "fulfilled clinical criteria for SPS; absence of lumbar lordosis on plain radiographs; collapse of L4 and L2 vertebrae due to lumbar paraspinal muscle spasms; presence of chronic inflammatory cells in pancreas associated with islets",
      "quote": "At presentation, she fulfilled clinical criteria for SPS (1,2). Supportive evidence for this diagnosis was the absence of lumbar lordosis in plain radiographs of the spine early in the course, the collapse of L4 and L2 vertebrae (thought to have been the result of lumbar paraspinal muscle spasms), and the presence of chronic inflammatory cells in the pancreas (some associated with islets) consistent with a reaction to anti-islet cell antibodies.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
